{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e20-scene-11",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Секрет шефа  (The Chef's Secret)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "nagiyev": "Нагиев",
  "vika": "Вика"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Nagiyev has called Barinov over to show him something on a phone: a video of the chef that has gone viral. Barinov assumes the worst, and is surprised by what he hears. Russian first, no need to catch it all.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Посмотри на это видео.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я не понимаю. Я уволен?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Нет, ты звезда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Почему я звезда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У видео миллион просмотров.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Все хотят видеть вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "У нас много гостей?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Да, все столики заняты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ты очень популярен сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Значит, я могу работать дальше?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Конечно! Иди на кухню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Спасибо, я пойду работать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Жду вкусный обед сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Будет сделано, мой босс.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Here it is again, piece by piece.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Посмотри на это видео.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Look at this video.' 'Look' is the informal order. 'Video' never changes, whatever its role.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я не понимаю. Я уволен?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't understand. Am I fired?' 'Fired' is a short masculine form, so no 'am'. The question lives on the voice.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Нет, ты звезда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, you're a star!' 'Star' is feminine. There's no 'are'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Почему я звезда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why am I a star?' The same word again, in the same shape. Barinov is baffled.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У видео миллион просмотров.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The video has a million views.' 'At the video' stands for 'has'. 'Million' is followed by the 'of' plural, 'views'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Все хотят видеть вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everyone wants to see you.' 'They want' finishes with 'yat'. 'You' takes the 'a' form, 'vas'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "У нас много гостей?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do we have many guests?' 'At us' stands for 'we have'. After 'many', 'guests' takes the 'ey' ending.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Да, все столики заняты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, all the tables are taken.' 'Taken' is a plural short form. 'Tables' are little tables, plural.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ты очень популярен сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You're very popular now.' 'Popular' is a short masculine form. 'Now' ends the line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Значит, я могу работать дальше?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'So can I go on working?' 'Can I' is one word. 'Further' means 'on'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Конечно! Иди на кухню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course! Go to the kitchen.' 'Go' is the informal order. 'To the kitchen' uses 'on' and a 'u' ending.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Спасибо, я пойду работать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thanks, I'll go and work.' 'I'll go' is a future form. 'Work' is the plain form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Жду вкусный обед сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I expect a tasty lunch today.' 'Wait' stands for 'expect'. 'Tasty lunch' has masculine endings.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Будет сделано, мой босс.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It'll be done, my boss.' 'Will be done' is a neuter short form. 'Boss' is borrowed. Now the whole conversation once more, from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Посмотри на это видео.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я не понимаю. Я уволен?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Нет, ты звезда!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Почему я звезда?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У видео миллион просмотров.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Все хотят видеть вас.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "У нас много гостей?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Да, все столики заняты.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ты очень популярен сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Значит, я могу работать дальше?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Конечно! Иди на кухню.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Спасибо, я пойду работать.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Жду вкусный обед сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Будет сделано, мой босс.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Barinov leaves with his job and his dignity intact. Remember that 'zvezda' means a star in the sky and a star in the film, and Russians use the one word for both. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "До свидания!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
